course: dictionary
lesson: 13000
title: Extant: still existing today
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Extant is a formal word, so you will meet it in history books and science texts. It means still existing today, especially something very old. «The oldest extant map of the town is over two hundred years old.» The clues are oldest and over two hundred years old: the map is very old, and it has survived until now.
explain: In science, extant has a second meaning: still living, not extinct. «The dodo is extinct, but the tortoise is an extant species.» The dodo no longer exists, while the tortoise is still alive. Extinct is the opposite of extant, so it is a useful clue.
explain: When you meet a new word, swap in your meaning and check. Does «still existing today» fit the sentence? If yes, you have the right meaning. If not, look at the clues again or check a dictionary.
fact: Extant means still existing today, especially something very old.
fact: Extant is a formal word, so you will see it more in books, history and science than in everyday talk.
fact: Extinct is the opposite of extant: it means no longer alive or no longer existing.
fact: «Extant species» means a kind of plant or animal that is still alive today.
fact: Context clues such as «oldest» and «still» show that extant means existing now.
exercise: «The oldest extant map of the town is over two hundred years old.» What does extant mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Brand new and never used | Torn up and thrown away | *Still existing today
exercise: «The dodo is extinct, but the tortoise is an extant species.» Which word in this sentence is the opposite of extant? | tortoise | species | *extinct | tall
exercise: «Scientists found an extant frog in the forest, and it was alive and well.» Find and copy the word that means still alive, not extinct. | *extant | found | scientists | forest
test: «The extant castle walls still stand on the hill.» What does extant mean? | *Still existing today | Very small | Made of wood | Torn down last week
test: Ella says extant means extinct. Why is she wrong? | Extant means very new | *Extinct means no longer alive, the opposite of extant | Extant and extinct both mean gone forever | Extant is a type of dinosaur
exam: Which sentence uses extant correctly? | Yesterday the extant rain fell all day | I ate an extant sandwich for lunch | My extant bike is blue and fast | *The museum has an extant copy of the book from 1600.
